ype":"text","url":"/docs/glossary#buttons","content":"GRM Portal"},"237":{"id":"/docs/glossary-141","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary#buttons","content":"Words that are project data rather than interface text — category names like\n*Complaint*, issue types like *Web Form*, and department names — stay in the\nlanguage they were entered in when the project was set up. That is why you\nwill see English words on an otherwise Kinyarwanda screen."},"238":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Welcome","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"239":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"A plain-language guide to the Grievance Redress Mechanism (eGRM) — for the people who report problems and the people who resolve them."},"240":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#which-part-do-you-need","content":"Which part do you need?"},"241":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#how-a-complaint-moves","content":"How a complaint moves"},"242":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#it-is-reported","content":"It is reported"},"243":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#it-gets-a-tracking-code","content":"It gets a tracking code"},"244":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#it-is-reviewed-and-assigned","content":"It is reviewed and assigned"},"245":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#it-is-resolved","content":"It is resolved"},"246":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#about-the-language","content":"About the language"},"247":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"eGRM is how a problem gets reported, tracked, and fixed. A member of the\npublic raises a complaint; a government officer records it, routes it to the\nright person, and resolves it. Everyone can see where it stands."},"248":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"This guide assumes no technical background. Pick the description below that\nsounds like you."},"249":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#which-part-do-you-need","content":"<Card title=\"I want to report a problem\" description=\"Send a complaint from the public website, with or without giving your name, and check on it later. No account needed.\" href=\"/docs/citizen\" />"},"250":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#which-part-do-you-need","content":"<Card title=\"I record complaints from the public\" description=\"Field Officer — take a complaint in person, by phone or by SMS and enter it into the system correctly.\" href=\"/docs/staff/field-officer\" />"},"251":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#which-part-do-you-need","content":"<Card title=\"I assign and resolve complaints\" description=\"Reviewer or Supervisor — check new complaints, send them to the right officer, and record the outcome.\" href=\"/docs/staff/reviewer\" />"},"252":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#which-part-do-you-need","content":"<Card title=\"I set up and run the system\" description=\"Project Administrator — create a project, load regions, add staff, and decide how complaints are routed.\" href=\"/docs/staff/administrator\" />"},"253":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#how-a-complaint-moves","content":"Every complaint follows the same path, no matter how it arrives:"},"254":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#it-is-reported","content":"Someone submits it on the public website, or tells a field officer in person,\nby phone, by SMS, or through the mobile app. The officer records it for them."},"255":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#it-gets-a-tracking-code","content":"The system gives the complaint a code like `RDAP-260907-6503`. Anyone holding\nthat code can check the status without logging in."},"256":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#it-is-reviewed-and-assigned","content":"A reviewer confirms the details and sends it to the officer or department\nresponsible for that area."},"257":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#it-is-resolved","content":"The assigned officer investigates, records what was done, and closes it. The\nstatus visible to the public updates at the same time."},"258":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#about-the-language","content":"The system opens in **Kinyarwanda**. The public website also offers\n**English** and **Français**, and you can switch at any time using the\nselector in the top-right corner."},"259":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#about-the-language","content":"The public website screenshots in this guide show the **English** version, so\nthey match the English text around them. The staff screens are shown in\n**Kinyarwanda**, because that is what staff accounts on this system actually\ndisplay. Every staff label is also listed in English on the\nScreen labels page."},"260":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"page","content":"Project Administrator","breadcrumbs":["Docs","For staff","For staff"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator"},"261":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-0","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator","content":"Creating a project, loading its regions, adding staff, and deciding how complaints are routed."},"262":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-1","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-1--name-the-project","content":"Step 1 — Name the project"},"263":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-2","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-2--build-the-region-structure","content":"Step 2 — Build the region structure"},"264":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-3","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Steps 3 to 8 — Define the vocabulary"},"265":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-4","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-9--add-the-staff","content":"Step 9 — Add the staff"},"266":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-5","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-10-to-12--routing-time-limits-and-statuses","content":"Steps 10 to 12 — Routing, time limits and statuses"},"267":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-6","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-13--activate","content":"Step 13 — Activate"},"268":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-7","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#before-you-hand-it-over","content":"Before you hand it over"},"269":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-8","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/administrator#if-you-get-stuck","content":"If you get stuck"},"270":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-9","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator","content":"A project is the container for everything else — its regions, its categories,\nits staff, and its complaints. Setting one up is done through the **Project\nSetup Wizard**, which walks through the steps in order and saves as it goes."},"271":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-10","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator","content":"From the main screen, open **Imishinga → Tangiriza Umushinga Mushya**\n(*Projects → Start New Project*). To change a project that already exists,\nopen it and choose **Edit in Wizard**."},"272":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-11","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-1--name-the-project","content":"The title, an optional start and end date, and the locale — country, default\nlanguage, number and date format, time zone."},"273":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-12","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-1--name-the-project","content":"**Default Language** here sets the labels that both citizens and staff see.\nChoose it deliberately: changing it later changes the interface for everyone\non the project at once."},"274":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-13","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-2--build-the-region-structure","content":"This is the most important step in the whole setup, and the hardest to change\nafterwards."},"275":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-14","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-2--build-the-region-structure","content":"First define the **levels** — the tiers your administrative hierarchy has,\nsuch as Province, District, Sector, Cell."},"276":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-15","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-2--build-the-region-structure","content":"Then load the actual regions into those levels. They can be imported rather\nthan typed one by one."},"277":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-16","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-2--build-the-region-structure","content":"Every complaint is routed by its region, and every officer sees complaints\nbased on the region they are assigned to. If the structure is wrong or\nincomplete, complaints will reach the wrong office and officers will be unable\nto see work that belongs to them. Get this right before adding anyone."},"278":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-17","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"These steps set the lists people will choose from. Each is a simple table you\nadd rows to."},"279":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-18","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Step"},"280":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-19","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"What it defines"},"281":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-20","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"User types"},"282":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-21","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"The kinds of staff account the project has"},"283":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-22","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Departments"},"284":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-23","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"The units that complaints can be assigned to"},"285":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-24","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Categories"},"286":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-25","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"What a complaint can be about"},"287":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-26","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Issue types"},"288":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-27","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"The channels complaints arrive through"},"289":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-28","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Citizen groups"},"290":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-29","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"How complainants are grouped for reporting"},"291":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-30","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Notification templates"},"292":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-31","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"The wording of the messages the system sends"},"293":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-32","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-3-to-8--define-the-vocabulary","content":"Keep these lists short. A category list with thirty entries produces\ninconsistent filing, because two officers will classify the same complaint\ndifferently."},"294":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-33","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-9--add-the-staff","content":"Users can be added one at a time, or loaded in bulk from a file."},"295":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-34","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-9--add-the-staff","content":"For a bulk load, upload the file, map its columns to the fields eGRM expects,\ncheck the preview, and confirm."},"296":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-35","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-9--add-the-staff","content":"**An account by itself grants nothing.** What determines which complaints a\nperson can see is the **region they are assigned to** — not their role. Staff\nin this system typically hold the same set of duties as each other and differ\nonly by region. A new user with no region assignment signs in successfully and\nsees an empty system."},"297":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-36","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-9--add-the-staff","content":"Check the preview before confirming a bulk import. Correcting a bad import is\nconsiderably more work than reading the preview."},"298":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-37","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-10-to-12--routing-time-limits-and-statuses","content":"**Routing** decides which department or role receives a complaint, based on\nits category and region."},"299":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-38","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-10-to-12--routing-time-limits-and-statuses","content":"**Time limits** set how long each stage may take before a complaint escalates\non its own."},"300":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-39","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-10-to-12--routing-time-limits-and-statuses","content":"**Statuses** are the stages a complaint passes through. Some are marked as\n*final*, meaning the complaint is finished."},"301":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-40","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#steps-10-to-12--routing-time-limits-and-statuses","content":"Be careful with **final** statuses. Marking more than one status as final —\nfor example both *Resolved* and *Closed* — makes the end state of a complaint\nambiguous, and which one a resolved complaint lands in may not be the one you\nintended. Keep exactly one final status unless you have a firm reason\notherwise, and check the result on a test complaint afterwards."},"302":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-41","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#step-13--activate","content":"Activation opens the project for real complaints."},"303":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-42","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#before-you-hand-it-over","content":"Check each of these yourself rather than assuming:"},"304":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-43","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#before-you-hand-it-over","content":"Submit a test complaint through the public website and confirm it appears\nfor the officer who should receive it."},"305":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-44","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#before-you-hand-it-over","content":"Sign in as one ordinary staff account and confirm they see the complaints\nthey should — and not the ones they should not."},"306":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-45","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#before-you-hand-it-over","content":"Check the tracking page returns a sensible result for the test complaint's\ncode."},"307":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-46","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#before-you-hand-it-over","content":"Delete the test complaint before real use begins."},"308":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-47","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#if-you-get-stuck","content":"**A user sees nothing after signing in.** They have no region assignment.\nThis is the most common report by a wide margin."},"309":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-48","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#if-you-get-stuck","content":"**Complaints reach the wrong office.** Check the region structure first and\nthe routing rules second — a misplaced region explains most of these."},"310":{"id":"/docs/staff/administrator-49","page_id":"/docs/staff/administrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/administrator#if-you-get-stuck","content":"**A region is missing.** Add it at the right level; do not attach it to the\nwrong parent as a shortcut, because visibility for every officer above it\nfollows that parent."},"311":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","type":"page","content":"Field Officer","breadcrumbs":["Docs","For staff","For staff"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/field-officer"},"312":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-0","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer","content":"Recording a complaint that someone brings to you in person, by phone, by SMS or on paper."},"313":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-1","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Record a complaint"},"314":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-2","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#give-the-person-their-tracking-code","content":"Give the person their tracking code"},"315":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-3","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#ask-before-you-write","content":"Ask before you write"},"316":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-4","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#checking-on-what-you-have-recorded","content":"Checking on what you have recorded"},"317":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-5","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#if-you-get-stuck","content":"If you get stuck"},"318":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-6","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer","content":"Most complaints do not arrive through the website. Someone stops you at a\nmeeting, calls the office, or sends an SMS. Your job is to get that into the\nsystem accurately, so it reaches the right officer and the person can follow\nit up."},"319":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-7","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"From the sidebar, click **Andika Ikibazo** (*Record Issue*)."},"320":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-8","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Fill in the form:"},"321":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-9","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Field (Kinyarwanda)"},"322":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-10","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"English"},"323":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-11","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"What to put"},"324":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-12","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Umushinga"},"325":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-13","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Project"},"326":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-14","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"The project this belongs to"},"327":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-15","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Icyiciro"},"328":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-16","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Category"},"329":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-17","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Complaint, Service Issue, Question or Other"},"330":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-18","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Ubwoko bw'Ikibazo"},"331":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-19","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Issue Type"},"332":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-20","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"**How it reached you** — In Person, Phone Call, SMS, Email, Verbal, Written"},"333":{"id":"/docs/staff/field-officer-21","page_id":"/docs/staff/field-officer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/staff/field-officer#record-a-complaint","content":"Itariki y'Ikibazo"},"334":{"id":"/docs/