0":172,"401":207,"402":89,"403":259,"404":389,"405":91,"406":146,"407":153,"408":251,"409":255,"410":180,"411":204,"412":262,"413":320,"414":275,"415":177,"416":178,"417":7,"418":430,"419":112,"420":22,"421":21,"422":118,"423":453,"424":79,"425":461,"426":419,"427":18,"428":19,"429":132,"430":468,"431":227,"432":1,"433":28,"434":43,"435":359,"436":212,"437":357,"438":393,"439":458,"440":233,"441":364,"442":201,"443":78,"444":421,"445":44,"446":279,"447":173,"448":356,"449":351,"450":239,"451":301,"452":82,"453":209,"454":97,"455":333,"456":216,"457":316,"458":223,"459":291,"460":40,"461":473,"462":398,"463":345,"464":234,"465":327,"466":382,"467":188,"468":136,"469":344,"470":354,"471":324,"472":58,"473":56,"474":2},"orderedDocs":[[92,"**\"Not found\" or no result.** Check the code character by character — the\nletters are the project code and the digits include the date. It is easy to\nread `0` as `O`."],[432,"**A complaint is in the wrong region.** Correct the region, then reassign.\nChanging the assignee alone leaves the routing wrong for next time."],[474,"**A complaint you expect is missing.** You only see complaints for the\nregions you are assigned to. If it belongs to a neighbouring district, it\nwill not appear for you."],[310,"**A region is missing.** Add it at the right level; do not attach it to the\nwrong parent as a shortcut, because visibility for every officer above it\nfollows that parent."],[308,"**A user sees nothing after signing in.** They have no region assignment.\nThis is the most common report by a wide margin."],[296,"**An account by itself grants nothing.** What determines which complaints a\nperson can see is the **region they are assigned to** — not their role. Staff\nin this system typically hold the same set of duties as each other and differ\nonly by region. A new user with no region assignment signs in successfully and\nsees an empty system."],[36,"**Category** — what your complaint is about:"],[417,"**Citizen Information may be empty, and that is deliberate.** People are\nallowed to report anonymously. An empty contact tab is not a data problem and\nis not something to chase — it means nobody may be called about this\ncomplaint, and the outcome has to be published through the tracking code\ninstead."],[87,"**Closed**"],[39,"**Complaint**"],[309,"**Complaints reach the wrong office.** Check the region structure first and\nthe routing rules second — a misplaced region explains most of these."],[273,"**Default Language** here sets the labels that both citizens and staff see.\nChoose it deliberately: changing it later changes the interface for everyone\non the project at once."],[53,"**Description** — what happened, where, and how it affected you. At least\n10 characters, up to 5,000."],[18,"**English**"],[19,"**Français**"],[332,"**How it reached you** — In Person, Phone Call, SMS, Email, Verbal, Written"],[59,"**I want updates**"],[355,"**Ibibazo Bifunguye** (*Open Issues*) in the sidebar lists complaints that are\nstill active."],[427,"**Igenzura → Ibyitwajwe** (*Supervision → Escalated*) — complaints raised to\na higher level, usually because they passed their time limit or needed\nauthority the assigned officer did not have."],[428,"**Igitekerezo → Ubujurire** (*Feedback → Appeals*) — where someone has come\nback dissatisfied with the outcome."],[83,"**In Progress**"],[421,"**Is the category right?** A \"Question\" misfiled as a \"Complaint\" enters a\nresolution process it never needed."],[420,"**Is the region right?** Routing follows the region on the complaint. If it\nis wrong, the complaint sits with an office that cannot act on it."],[47,"**Issue Type** — how you are reporting it. Choosing from the website, pick\n**Web Form**. The other options (In Person, Phone Call, SMS, Email, Verbal,\nWritten, Mobile App) are used by officers recording a complaint on someone\nelse's behalf."],[345,"**Issue Type** records the channel the complaint arrived through, not how\nserious it is. If someone telephoned you, choose **Phone Call** — not\n**Web Form**, even though you are typing it into a web page. These figures are\nused to decide which channels the public actually rely on."],[17,"**Kinyarwanda** (the default)"],[81,"**New**"],[48,"**Next** stays grey until you have picked one of each."],[433,"**Nobody is available in the assigned department.** Reassign to another\nofficer rather than leaving it unassigned — an unassigned complaint has no\nowner and will not be picked up by anyone."],[45,"**Other**"],[43,"**Question**"],[89,"**Rejected**"],[85,"**Resolved**"],[298,"**Routing** decides which department or role receives a complaint, based on\nits category and region."],[41,"**Service Issue**"],[372,"**Someone reports the same problem twice.** Record it anyway and mention the\nearlier tracking code in the description. A reviewer will merge them."],[300,"**Statuses** are the stages a complaint passes through. Some are marked as\n*final*, meaning the complaint is finished."],[57,"**Stay anonymous**"],[61,"**Stay anonymous** is selected by default. Either way you still get a tracking\ncode, and you can still check the status yourself at any time."],[12,"**Submit a Complaint → Start form**"],[460,"**The cards in the middle** group everything else by the kind of work it\nbelongs to — intake, feedback, supervision, projects, users, and system\nsettings. You will only be able to open the ones your role allows."],[66,"**The Next button stays grey.** A required field on that step is still\nempty. On step 1 you need both a category and an issue type; on step 3 the\ndescription must be at least 10 characters."],[370,"**The region you need is not in the list.** Choose the nearest level above\nit and name the exact place in the description. Then tell your administrator\nthe region is missing."],[434,"**The same problem is reported twice.** Resolve one and record the other's\ntracking code in the outcome, so both codes give the person a real answer."],[445,"**The sidebar on the left** is always there. Its entries are:"],[94,"**The status has not changed in a long time.** Contact the office handling\nthe project and quote your tracking code."],[299,"**Time limits** set how long each stage may take before a complaint escalates\non its own."],[14,"**Track a Complaint → Enter code**"],[353,"**What specifically went wrong**, in the person's own words rather than a\nsummary like \"service problem\"."],[52,"**When did this happen?** — the date of the problem. Today's date is filled\nin already; change it if the problem happened earlier."],[352,"**When exactly.** A date, even an approximate one."],[351,"**Where exactly.** A village or facility name, not just a district. This is\nwhat decides who receives it."],[354,"**Whether they want to be contacted.** If they do, take a phone number. If\nthey would rather not be named, that is their right — record it anonymously\nand say so."],[68,"**You closed the page mid-way.** Nothing is saved until you press\n**Submit Complaint**, so start again from the beginning."],[93,"**You lost the code.** If you gave contact details when you submitted, the\noffice can look your complaint up for you. If you chose to stay anonymous,\nthere is no way to recover it — you would need to submit again."],[371,"**You saved it with the wrong details.** Open the complaint and use\n**Reassign Issue** for the wrong owner, or ask a reviewer for anything else\n— once submitted, some fields are locked to keep the record trustworthy."],[473,"**You sign in but see almost nothing.** You have an account but no region\nassignment yet. Until an administrator assigns you to a region, there are no\ncomplaints you are allowed to see."],[67,"**Your location is not in the list.** Choose the closest area above it and\nname the exact place in the description instead."],[472,"**Your password does not work.** Passwords are not shown to anyone, so a\nreset is the only fix — ask your administrator."],[24,"<Card title=\"Check a complaint\" description=\"Use your tracking code to see the current status.\" href=\"/docs/citizen/track\" />"],[251,"<Card title=\"I assign and resolve complaints\" description=\"Reviewer or Supervisor — check new complaints, send them to the right officer, and record the outcome.\" href=\"/docs/staff/reviewer\" />"],[250,"<Card title=\"I record complaints from the public\" description=\"Field Officer — take a complaint in person, by phone or by SMS and enter it into the system correctly.\" href=\"/docs/staff/field-officer\" />"],[252,"<Card title=\"I set up and run the system\" description=\"Project Administrator — create a project, load regions, add staff, and decide how complaints are routed.\" href=\"/docs/staff/administrator\" />"],[249,"<Card title=\"I want to report a problem\" description=\"Send a complaint from the public website, with or without giving your name, and check on it later. No account needed.\" href=\"/docs/citizen\" />"],[23,"<Card title=\"Send a complaint\" description=\"A four-step form. Takes a few minutes.\" href=\"/docs/citizen/submit\" />"],[26,"A four-step form on the public website. You can send it without giving your name."],[239,"A plain-language guide to the Grievance Redress Mechanism (eGRM) — for the people who report problems and the people who resolve them."],[270,"A project is the container for everything else — its regions, its categories,\nits staff, and its complaints. Setting one up is done through the **Project\nSetup Wizard**, which walks through the steps in order and saves as it goes."],[256,"A reviewer confirms the details and sends it to the officer or department\nresponsible for that area."],[42,"A service is not working, is late, or is unavailable"],[140,"Abakoresha & Uburenganzira"],[142,"Abakoresha ku Mushinga"],[246,"About the language"],[222,"Actions"],[302,"Activation opens the project for real complaints."],[220,"Add"],[147,"Administrative Level Types"],[175,"Administrative Region"],[443,"After signing in you land on the **eG