ing the language changes the labels and buttons. It does not change\nanything about your complaint, and you can switch back at any time."],[69,"Check a complaint"],[13,"Check a problem I already reported"],[429,"Check both regularly. Neither will come to you as a notification if you are\nnot assigned to the individual complaint."],[303,"Check each of these yourself rather than assuming:"],[297,"Check the preview before confirming a bulk import. Correcting a bad import is\nconsiderably more work than reading the preview."],[306,"Check the tracking page returns a sensible result for the test complaint's\ncode."],[468,"Checking new complaints and sending them to the right person"],[374,"Checking new complaints, sending them to the right officer, recording the outcome, and handling escalations."],[316,"Checking on what you have recorded"],[37,"Choice"],[55,"Choice"],[232,"Choose / Select"],[49,"Choose the area the problem relates to, starting from the top level and\nworking down. Each choice you make reveals the next level, so keep selecting\nuntil there are no more lists to fill."],[30,"Choose whether to give your contact details"],[289,"Citizen groups"],[185,"Citizen Information"],[406,"Citizen Information"],[62,"Click **Submit Complaint** to finish."],[397,"Click any row."],[72,"Click Track Complaint"],[205,"Closed"],[329,"Complaint, Service Issue, Question or Other"],[392,"Complaints assigned to you personally"],[407,"Contact details, if any were given"],[216,"Continue / Next"],[261,"Creating a project, loading its regions, adding staff, and deciding how complaints are routed."],[307,"Delete the test complaint before real use begins."],[283,"Departments"],[29,"Describe what happened"],[165,"Description"],[340,"Description"],[151,"Duty Catalogue"],[247,"eGRM is how a problem gets reported, tracked, and fixed. A member of the\npublic raises a complaint; a government officer records it, routes it to the\nright person, and resolves it. Everyone can see where it stands."