,[124,"Kwakira"],[226,"Log in"],[194,"Meaning"],[359,"Meaning"],[234,"Mobile App"],[318,"Most complaints do not arrive through the website. Someone stops you at a\nmeeting, calls the office, or sends an SMS. Your job is to get that into the\nsystem accurately, so it reaches the right officer and the person can follow\nit up."],[119,"My Assignments"],[391,"My Assignments"],[459,"My Assignments"],[97,"Navigation"],[196,"New"],[361,"New"],[6,"Next"],[46,"None of the above fits"],[209,"Not taken forward"],[90,"Not taken forward — usually because it falls outside what this mechanism covers, or there was not enough information to act on."],[291,"Notification templates"],[111,"Notifications"],[451,"Notifications"],[227,"Ohereza"],[104,"On screen"],[122,"On screen"],[152,"On screen"],[180,"On screen"],[192,"On screen"],[213,"On screen"],[219,"Ongeraho"],[33,"Open **egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal** and\nclick **Submit a Complaint → Start form**, or **Submit** in the top menu."],[8,"Open **egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal**."],[76,"Open **egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal/track**,\nor click **Track** in the top menu."],[376,"Open a complaint"],[115,"Open Issues"],[388,"Open Issues"],[457,"Open Issues"],[211,"Pending"],[357,"Pill"],[233,"Porogaramu ya Telefoni"],[413,"Progress against the complaint"],[155,"Project"],[325,"Project"],[260,"Project Administrator"],[471,"Project Administrator"],[143,"Project Users"],[135,"Projects"],[465,"Read"],[348,"Read this code back to the person, and make sure they have written it down,\nbefore they leave or you end the call. If they gave no contact details, this\ncode is the only way they can ever check their complaint again."],[82,"Received, waiting for an officer to review it."],[313,"Record a complaint"],[113,"Record Issue"],[394,"Record Issue"],[455,"Record Issue"],[378,"Record the outcome"],[197,"Recorded, not yet reviewed"],[362,"Recorded, not yet reviewed"],[312,"Recording a complaint that someone brings to you in person, by phone, by SMS or on paper."],[343,"Region"],[208,"Rejected"],[11,"Report a new problem"],[202,"Resolved"],[367,"Resolved"],[373,"Reviewer and Supervisor"],[469,"Reviewer and Supervisor"],[463,"Roles in eGRM are about **duties**, and most staff hold several at once. What\nactually differs between two officers is usually the **region** they are\nassigned to, not the buttons they can press."],[347,"Saving produces a tracking code like `RDAP-260907-6503`."],[27,"Say what kind of problem it is"],[28,"Say where it happened"],[95,"Screen labels"],[109,"Search"],[449,"Search"],[98,"Sections of the main screen"],[25,"Send a complaint"],[470,"Setting up projects, regions and staff accounts"],[108,"Shakisha"],[448,"Shakisha"],[437,"Sign in"],[305,"Sign in as one ordinary staff account and confirm they see the complaints\nthey should — and not the ones they should not."],[435,"Signing in"],[144,"Sisitemu"],[254,"Someone submits it on the public website, or tells a field officer in person,\nby phone, by SMS, or through the mobile app. The officer records it for them."],[40,"Something went wrong and you want it put right"],[103,"Staff screens on this system display in Kinyarwanda. If you are reading this\nguide in English, use this page to match what is on your screen to what is\nwritten here."],[441,"Staff work in a different part of the system from the public website. You need\nan account, which an administrator creates for you."],[139,"Start New Project"],[79,"Status"],[163,"Status"],[101,"Statuses"],[279,"Step"],[262,"Step 1 — Name the project"],[267,"Step 13 — Activate"],[263,"Step 2 — Build the region structure"],[265,"Step 9 — Add the staff"],[266,"Steps 10 to 12 — Routing, time limits and statuses"],[264,"Steps 3 to 8 — Define the vocabulary"],[217,"Subira inyuma"],[228,"Submit"],[304,"Submit a test complaint through the public website and confirm it appears\nfor the officer who should receive it."],[131,"Supervision"],[145,"System"],[100,"Tabs on a complaint"],[466,"Taking complaints from the public and entering them"],[138,"Tangiriza Umushinga Mushya"],[349,"Tell them they can check it at **egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal** under\n**Track**, and that it will show the status but not their description."],[22,"The **Mobile App** link is for field officers who collect complaints in places\nwith no internet. As a member of the public you do not need it — the website\ndoes everything you need."],[257,"The assigned officer investigates, records what was done, and closes it. The\nstatus visible to the public updates at the same time."],[288,"The channels complaints arrive through"],[356,"The coloured pill in the **Imimerere** (*Status*) column shows where each one\nhas got to:"],[404,"The complaint itself — dates, category, description, region, status"],[34,"The form has four steps. A row of dots at the top shows how far along you are,\nand **Back** always returns to the previous step without losing what you typed."],[282,"The kinds of staff account the project has"],[396,"The list shows the tracking code, the status pill, and the reference. The grey\nboxes along the top filter it — by project, category, department, assignee,\nissue type, status or region. Newly arrived complaints carry the\n**Gishya** (*New*) pill."],[438,"The main screen"],[86,"The officer has recorded an outcome."],[326,"The project this belongs to"],[259,"The public website screenshots in this guide show the **English** version, so\nthey match the English text around them. The staff screens are shown in\n**Kinyarwanda**, because that is what staff accounts on this system actually\ndisplay. Every staff label is also listed in English on the\nScreen labels page."],[350,"The quality of a complaint depends almost entirely on what you capture at this\nmoment. Before you save, check you have:"],[462,"The staff screens display in **Kinyarwanda**, because that is the language\nthis system is set to. The Screen labels page lists every\nlabel you will meet with its English meaning. If you would rather work in\nEnglish, ask your administrator to set the language on your own account — it\nchanges only what you see, not what anyone else sees."],[255,"The system gives the complaint a code like `RDAP-260907-6503`. Anyone holding\nthat code can check the status without logging in."],[258,"The system opens in **Kinyarwanda**. The public website also offers\n**English** and **Français**, and you can switch at any time using the\nselector in the top-right corner."],[398,"The tabs across the top separate the record into sections:"],[272,"The title, an optional start and end date, and the locale — country, default\nlanguage, number and date format, time zone."],[91,"The tracking page deliberately shows only the status, category and submission\ndate. It does not show your description, your contact details, or the names of\nthe officers involved. This is so that a tracking code shared with or\noverheard by someone else cannot expose personal information."],[3,"The two things you can do"],[284,"The units that complaints can be assigned to"],[16,"The website opens in Kinyarwanda. To read it in another language, use the\nselector at the **top-right** of any page. Three choices are available:"],[292,"The wording of the messages the system sends"],[276,"Then load the actual regions into those levels. They can be imported rather\nthan typed one by one."],[346,"Then save."],[65,"Then see Check a complaint."],[278,"These steps set the lists people will choose from. Each is a simple table you\nadd rows to."],[248,"This guide assumes no technical background. Pick the description below that\nsounds like you."],[77,"This is the code you were given when you submitted, in the form\n`RDAP-260907-6503`. Type it exactly, including the dashes."],[274,"This is the most important step in the whole setup, and the hardest to change\nafterwards."],[50,"This is what decides which office receives your complaint, so pick the place\nthe problem actually happened — not where you live, if they are differe